# THE PARKING PROTOTYPE'S ENGINE (docs/notes/parking-prototype.md; operator,
# 2026-11-24, relayed from the architecture session: parking step 1, "N park
# cycles the same bytes; the park, the un-park and the first request timed
# apart; the parked process's floor read"). The candidate engine-fixes.series
# and TWO patches more: 0015, weights that leave the device and come back;
# 0016, a test switch that refuses a pool's growth on demand (the pool's
# refusal, 0013, could not be provoked by filling the card).
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/parking-prototype.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>
# INSTALLED BESIDE THE LIVE ENGINE AND NEVER SWAPPED: one copy of bge-m3 uses
# it, direct, with three env lines (a reranker copy with one, for 0016's
# check). Without those lines it is the fixes'
# engine. It may be rebuilt as the prototype is corrected; no gate depends
# on it, and no vector written to a collection comes from it.
